  semgrep     — Static analysis for many languages
               Install: pip install semgrep

  codeql      — Deep code analysis by GitHub
               Install: https://github.com/github/codeql-cli-binaries

  slither     — Solidity smart contract analyzer
               Install: pip install slither-analyzer

  libfuzzer   — Coverage-guided fuzzing (requires Clang)
               Install: apt install clang (Linux) / brew install llvm (macOS)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
🤖 AI PROVIDERS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  The agent supports 5 AI providers with automatic fallback:

  Provider       Key Variable              Free Tier         Local?
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Gemini         GEMINI_API_KEY            1500 req/day      No
  Groq           GROQ_API_KEY              30 req/min        No
  HuggingFace    HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY       1000 req/day      No
  OpenRouter     OPENROUTER_API_KEY        Varies by model   No
  Ollama         (none — runs locally)     Unlimited         Yes

  📍 WHERE TO RUN COMMANDS:
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Step 1: Open Terminal

  Step 2: Navigate to the agent directory:
          cd cyber-guardians-mobile/cyberguard-agent

  Step 3: Set your API key (one of these):

          # Gemini (Google AI Studio)
          export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key-here"
          Get key from: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey

          # Groq (Console)
          export GROQ_API_KEY="your-key-here"
          Get key from: https://console.groq.com/keys

          # HuggingFace (Settings)
          export HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY="your-key-here"
          Get key from: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens

          # OpenRouter (Keys)
          export OPENROUTER_API_KEY="your-key-here"
          Get key from: https://openrouter.ai/keys

          # Ollama (No key needed!)
          curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh
          ollama pull llama3.2

  Step 4: Start the agent:
          npm start

  💡 TIP: Add export commands to ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc to persist them:

          echo 'export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key"' >> ~/.bashrc
          source ~/.bashrc

  📌 IMPORTANT: Always run commands from the agent directory:
     /cyber-guardians-mobile/cyberguard-agent/

     NOT from the game root directory!
     NOT from inside src/ or bin/!

